    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/parking-control-officer-manhattan-kansas-united-states-1bb7ebb7-b28d-48aa-95f2-ef0d767aea59": {
      "title": "Parking Control Officer",
      "description": "Parking Control Officer - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Parking Control Officer - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Parking Control Officer Apply Now Parking Control Officer The position is a Parking Control Officer. The position includes writing tickets on vehicles that are in violation of Parking Rules and Regulations, towing of vehicles that are excessive or illegally parked and working special events such as football games. 522425 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Parking Services Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Nov 9 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The position is a Parking Control Officer. The position includes: writing tickets on vehicles that are in violation of Parking Rules and Regulations, towing of vehicles that are excessive or illegally parked and working special events such as football games. Extensive training is given to each employee when they start working and staff meetings are held. Employee is expected to work with little or no supervision most of the time. About Us Kansas State University’s Parking Services Department is dedicated to providing efficient, customer-focused parking and transportation solutions that support the university’s mission. We manage a comprehensive system of parking resources, including permits, enforcement, and alternative transportation options, to ensure a safe and accessible campus for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Our team is committed to continuous improvement, leveraging technology and innovative strategies to enhance the campus experience. Through a service-first approach, we strive to balance the needs of the campus community while promoting sustainability and mobility. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent). Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications: One year of parking services or relevant work experience. Good written and oral communications skills. Customer service experience preferred. Good organizational abilities. Additional Role Information: Upon employment, training with new software, hardware, and equipment adapted by the department is required. Work occasionally requires moderate to considerable physical exertion handling snow and ice melt during inclement weather. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Application Resume Application Window Applications close on: November 9, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range Hourly $ 16.36 - $20.44 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) dd1b77ce Last Name (required) f80555e7 Email (required) ee23058f Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: b73299c7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Event Management / Services Administrative / Professional Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Event Management / Services Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 9233c660 Last Name (required) a0bc30ff Save t