    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/graphic-designer-manhattan-kansas-united-states-fbe47b9b-8015-41c0-8188-27f2411c0c72": {
      "title": "Graphic Designer",
      "description": "Graphic Designer - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Graphic Designer - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Graphic Designer Apply Now Graphic Designer Housed within the Division of Communications and Marketing, or DCM, this position serves a wide range of partners across K-State, including the university’s 11 colleges, the Office of the President, statewide extension offices, researchers, specialists and university administrators. The position will support a mix of DCM projects across print and digital channels. 522408 Manhattan, Kansas, United States 3670006010 Div Comm and Mrktg Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Nov 11 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role Housed within the Division of Communications and Marketing, or DCM, this position serves a wide range of partners across K-State, including the university’s 11 colleges, the Office of the President, statewide extension offices, researchers, specialists and university administrators. The position will support a mix of DCM projects across print and digital channels. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong visual communication abilities across multiple formats and platforms. The successful candidate will be a creative, results-oriented designer who works well with partners from across the university and other marketing and communications professionals. They will meet directly with clients to understand their goals, translate those needs into effective design solutions and manage projects from concept through completion. All work should reflect K-State and K-State Research and Extension brand standards. About Us Kansas State University’s Division of Communications and Marketing (DCM) brings together strategists, storytellers and creative professionals to strengthen K-State’s reputation, support enrollment and advance university priorities. We partner with colleges, departments and leadership across the university to turn complex ideas into clear messages and compelling experiences through marketing, communications, design, web, photography, video and media relations. Our work connects audiences with the people, opportunities and discoveries that make K-State a distinctive choice for students and a vital partner to Kansas and the world. Our priorities include: Support student recruitment and enrollment by showing how K-State’s academic programs, applied learning and student experiences prepare students for what’s next. Build K-State’s reputation by sharing the people, discoveries and partnerships advancing solutions in community health, sustainability, food security, biosecurity and technology. Connect K-State’s expertise to Kansas communities through collaboration with K-State Research and Extension, demonstrating the university’s role in improving lives and livelihoods across the state. Keep university audiences informed and engaged through timely, clear communications that support institutional initiatives and help people understand and navigate change. Create a consistent, compelling K-State experience across campaigns, websites, stories and visual content. Strengthen collaboration across campus by helping partners define goals, understand audiences and develop coordinated marketing and communications plans. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and four years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of work experience and education. Preferred Qualifications: Five-Seven years of experience as a graphic designer or similar position. Strong editing skills and attention to detail are critical. Two or more years working with and developing projects for clients. Experience with illustration, motion graphics/animation or other specialized design fields. Background in brand development or logo/identity design. Experience with publications and layout work. Experience with an online project management system. Excellent communicator with strong written communication skills and the ability to communicate well. Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, team-driven environment. This position uses a computer, printer and various design production equipment, sitting for extended periods of time. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Design Portfolio (website or PDF preferred) Three References Application Window Applications close on: November 11th, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $ 42,216.00 - $ 53,819.00 Annually Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) cbd72a97 Last Name (required) 23b7b0f1 Email (required) f80ef6b3 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 1c45fdf2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Communications / Public Relations / Marketing Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 7588545a Last Name (required) 294057af Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later c2938