    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/custodial-specialist-manhattan-kansas-united-states-b6c6d3cc-6155-4e00-a91f-2a2cbf1d6135": {
      "title": "Custodial Specialist",
      "description": "Custodial Specialist - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Custodial Specialist - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Custodial Specialist Apply Now Custodial Specialist Sparkle and shine as part of a cohesive cleaning team that provides services to K-State residence halls. The team ensures clean and appealing facilities for students and guests. Work hours are 7:30am-4:00pm, M-F. 522393 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Department of Housing & Dining Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Nov 9 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role Join the K-State Housing and Dining Services team to help maintain clean, safe, and welcoming residence halls and facilities. This position supports the comfort and well-being of students, faculty, staff, and guests by keeping spaces clean, sanitary, organized, and presentable. Duties may also include providing housekeeping services for university guests and conference groups. Duties and Responsibilities include: • Perform routine cleaning tasks, including taking out trash, vacuuming, dusting, sweeping, and mopping floors. • Clean and disinfect surfaces, fixtures, and restrooms to maintain sanitary conditions. • Help keep residence halls and other facilities clean, organized, safe, and welcoming. • Provide basic housekeeping services for university guests and conference groups as needed. • Assist with minor maintenance and other cleaning-related tasks. • Work cooperatively with team members to complete daily assignments. • Perform other duties as assigned, including assisting in other areas or covering for absent employees. • Attend training sessions, conferences, or workshops as needed. About Us Housing and Dining Services is a large, self-operated auxiliary department serving more than 5,000 students that call the K-State campus home. This \"home away from home\" meets more than the basic needs of students living with us — we provide affordable, safe and engaging accommodations and services for our residents, while finding unique ways to support them in their academic pursuits. We pride ourselves on taking excellent care of our residents, and that is reflected in our recent Princeton Review rankings. The 2025 Princeton Review ranks us #2 Happiest Students, #2 Best Quality of Life, #8 Best College Residence Halls, and #14 Best Campus Food. YOU can help make our residents and guests feel welcome and comfortable! Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Preferred Qualifications: Some experience in cleaning or housekeeping. Ability to understand and follow oral and written instructions. Learn the operation and care of vacuum cleaners, scrubbing machines, polishing machines and other janitorial equipment. Ability to work harmoniously and effectively with others and to communicate effectively both orally and in writing. Additional Role Information: Bloodborne Pathogens training to be completed upon employment. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Online application Application Window Applications close on: November 9, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $15.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 3ec8fde6 Last Name (required) 0d0cf123 Email (required) 3bb61085 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: f80728ba Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) bc42f1f1 Last Name (required) 08a1ed5b Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later c66b8a4d Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 201d0f30 Last Name (required) 3c6457b4 Email (required) ad371051 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 92b3dbd8 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Graphic Designer Manhattan 3670006010 Div Comm and Mrktg Marketing & Member Strategist Other AQ Miller Schl of Media & Comm Landscape Technician II Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sa