    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/veterinary-assistant-float-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Veterinary Assistant - Float",
      "description": "Veterinary Assistant - Float - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Veterinary Assistant - Float - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Veterinary Assistant - Float Apply Now Veterinary Assistant - Float The Veterinary Health Center (VHC) within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking applicants for a Patient Float Veterinary Assistant. The purpose of this position is to provide quality customer service from the time of arrival to when the patient goes home, and to provide help with patient care throughout the hospital as needed in various departments. This position will provide help with patient intake, transporting patients throughout the hospital for a variety of services, aiding VHC veterinarians and Registered Veterinary Nurses in the performance of their duties to improve the efficiency of the hospital and improve client service experience. Hospital mission includes requirement of providing quality medical services to clients and training for professional veterinary students. 521854 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Veterinary Health Center Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Nov 9 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Veterinary Health Center (VHC) within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking a Veterinary Assistant to join our dedicated team to help facilitate exemplary patient care and quality customer service. This position will provide patient and administrative support to the faculty, staff, and veterinary students of the VHC. The role will include many engaging responsibilities such as overseeing patient intake, assisting with treatments, ensuring accuracy of visit charges, and providing quality customer service from patient check-in to discharge. Working hours for this position will include daytime hours Monday-Friday. Excellent communication skills and attention to detail will be key in succeeding in this position. About Us The Veterinary Health Center is a teaching hospital that offers routine, emergency, and specialty care services. The VHC strives to provide exceptional care for patients from high-quality routine healthcare to state-of-the-art advanced therapy for seriously ill patients. The Veterinary Health Center is located in Manhattan, Kansas which is a vibrant college community with a population of over 55,000 in the Flint Hills. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes 24 vacation days plus other paid time off (holidays, sick, and discretionary), health insurance, life insurance, and retirement plans. To see what benefits are available, please visit: www.ksvhc.org/about/employment/recruitment.html Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) One year of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: 1 year or more experience as a veterinary assistant. Experience working with electronic medical records systems. Ability to handle, restrain, and provide medical treatments to domestic animals. Experience in client services. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Contact information for three professional references Application Window Applications close on: 11/9/2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $15.50-$17.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 205dc7e0 Last Name (required) c5ebd09a Email (required) d58d052b Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: c96f8470 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns 