    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/animal-technician-i-large-animal-manhattan-kansas-united-states-9bed6237-816f-4a3e-be86-ebb5f469f83b": {
      "title": "Animal Technician I - Large Animal",
      "description": "Animal Technician I - Large Animal - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Animal Technician I - Large Animal - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Animal Technician I - Large Animal Apply Now Animal Technician I - Large Animal The Veterinary Health Center (VHC) within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking an Animal Technician I to join our dedicated team to help facilitate exemplary patient care and quality customer service. This position supports the routine and specialized care of hospitalized animals in the Veterinary Health Center at Kansas State University by maintaining and ensuring a sanitary and safe environment for patients, faculty, staff, students, and visitors. At the discretion of clinicians and clinical staff, this position will tend to the feeding and general welfare of VHC clients. This position is responsible for the cleaning and disinfecting of large animal areas and equipment of the hospital. Ensure the large animal facilities meet federal, state, and VHC standards for cleanliness and sanitation. Working hours for this position will include Monday-Friday, 12:00am-8:00am. 521515 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Veterinary Health Center Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Nov 16 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Veterinary Health Center (VHC) within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking an Animal Technician I to join our dedicated team to help facilitate exemplary patient care and quality customer service. This position supports the routine and specialized care of hospitalized animals in the Veterinary Health Center at Kansas State University by maintaining and ensuring a sanitary and safe environment for patients, faculty, staff, students, and visitors. At the discretion of clinicians and clinical staff, this position will tend to the feeding and general welfare of VHC clients. This position is responsible for the cleaning and disinfecting of large animal areas and equipment of the hospital. Ensure the large animal facilities meet federal, state, and VHC standards for cleanliness and sanitation. Working hours for this position will include Monday-Friday, 12:00am-8:00am. About Us The Veterinary Health Center is a teaching hospital that offers routine, emergency, and specialty care services. The VHC strives to provide exceptional care for patients from high-quality routine healthcare to state-of-the-art advanced therapy for seriously ill patients. The Veterinary Health Center is located in Manhattan, Kansas which is a vibrant college community with a population of over 55,000 in the Flint Hills. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes 24 vacation days plus other paid time off (holidays, sick, and discretionary), health insurance, life insurance, and retirement plans. To see what benefits are available, please visit: www.ksvhc.org/about/employment/recruitment.html Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with large animals. One year of relevant experience. High school diploma Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. Resume 2. Cover Letter 3. Contact information for three professional references Application Window Applications close: November 16, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $15.50-$16.50/hr Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 6180dae3 Last Name (required) 2ac67a2d Email (required) f7ebe07a Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 69b96424 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 3a4214d1 Last Name (required) c0bd46b6 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 676b9036 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) d44f6436 Last Name (required) d73108bf Email (required) 6b5bb675 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job e1f68b04 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Extension Ag Economist- KFMA NW Colby Colby KS Farm Management Association System Support Specialist Manhattan Health & Human Sciences Dean Shawnee County 4‑H Youth Development Extension Agent Other Office of External Engagement Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area B