    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/custodial-specialist-manhattan-kansas-united-states-c9c681b2-e269-4d48-b319-247facb89ca7": {
      "title": "Custodial Specialist",
      "description": "Custodial Specialist - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Custodial Specialist - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Custodial Specialist Apply Now Custodial Specialist This position supports K-State’s mission of learning, scholarship, creative endeavor, and research by creating and maintaining an environment which contributes to the health and safety of students, faculty, staff, and visitors. 521489 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fac Custodial Services Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Nov 29 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position supports K-State’s mission of learning, scholarship, creative endeavor, and research by creating and maintaining an environment which contributes to the health and safety of students, faculty, staff, and visitors. This position plays an integral role in maintaining and sustaining university structural assets. This position is responsible for first impressions, thus playing an important role in student & faculty recruitment and retention. This position performs a variety of custodial functions to include cleaning, disinfecting, minor equipment repair and preventative maintenance. It will be required to utilize a broad array of chemicals and operate a variety of power equipment in maintenance of floors and other duties. The position will also perform a variety of miscellaneous tasks as assigned by leadership and must be able to work with minimal supervision. This position requires the ability to frequently interact effectively with university students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Direct supervision is from the Custodial Services Supervisor. Hours are 5:00 a.m. – 1:30, with occasional call back for emergencies About Us The Division of Facilities is an action-oriented service organization within the K-State family. We plan, budget, build, operate, maintain, clean, supply and transport. We are custodians, landscapers, carpenters, plumbers, electricians, mechanics, project managers, engineers, architects, accountants, and administrative professionals — all stewards and leaders of an inspiring campus shared by many. We wholeheartedly embrace the K-State traditions of excellence, integrity and professionalism, and we are enthusiastic champions of K-State's visionary goal to become a Top 50 Public Research University by 2025. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Preferred Qualifications: Ability to operate a wide variety of commercial janitorial equipment and understand/follow explicit instructions, both oral and written form. Additional Role Information: Could be called into work in emergency situations including but not limited to inclement weather, flooding caused by weather, accidents or infrastructure failure and recovery from other catastrophic events (tornado, fire, blood, etc.). Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. All candidates must be 18 years of age. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. Application 2. Resume Application Window Applications close on: November 29, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $15.00-16.00 + .60 Shift Differential (Hourly) Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 3718b551 Last Name (required) a7e0aa26 Email (required) 5080fecf Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: c0d7926c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) af353028 Last Name (required) abe98f68 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later bc6685c6 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 4781160e Last Name (required) 87748fd1 Email (required) 2dd412e8 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 04721867 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Extension Ag Economist- KFMA NW Colby Colby KS Farm Management Association System Support Specialist Manhattan Health & Human Sciences Dean Shawnee County 4‑H Youth Development Extension Agent Other Office of External Engagement Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125%