    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/veterinary-nurse-i-ii-or-iii-sa-icu-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Veterinary Nurse I,II, or III - SA ICU",
      "description": "Veterinary Nurse I,II, or III - SA ICU - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Veterinary Nurse I,II, or III - SA ICU - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Veterinary Nurse I,II, or III - SA ICU Apply Now Veterinary Nurse I,II, or III - SA ICU This position holds many engaging responsibilities including helping to provide vital care for critical patients, operating medical equipment, and performing or assisting in technical procedures. Nurses on this team assist in day-to-day responsibilities like monitoring medical records, organizing technical work, maintaining equipment and supply statuses, as well as coordinating animal treatments. Communication and collaboration skills will be utilized daily. Working hours for this position will be Wednesday-Friday, 3 p.m. to 3 a.m. and one Saturday overnight per month. 519130 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Veterinary Health Center Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Nov 10 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Veterinary Health Center (VHC) within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking an overnight Veterinary Nurse I, II, or III to join our dedicated Intensive Care Unit (ICU) team to help facilitate exemplary patient care. This position holds many engaging responsibilities including helping to provide vital care for critical patients, operating medical equipment, and performing or assisting in technical procedures. Nurses on this team assist in day-to-day responsibilities like monitoring medical records, organizing technical work, maintaining equipment and supply statuses, as well as coordinating animal treatments. Communication and collaboration skills will be utilized daily. Working hours for this position will be Wednesday-Friday, 3 p.m. to 3 a.m. and one Saturday overnight per month. About Us The Veterinary Health Center is a teaching hospital that offers routine, emergency, and specialty care services. The VHC strives to provide exceptional care for patients from high-quality routine healthcare to state-of-the-art advanced therapy for seriously ill patients. The Veterinary Health Center is located in Manhattan, Kansas which is a vibrant college community with a population of over 55,000 in the Flint Hills. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes 24 vacation days plus other paid time off (holidays, sick, and discretionary), health insurance, life insurance, and retirement plans. To see what benefits are available, please visit: www.ksvhc.org/about/employment/recruitment.html Worksite Option This position is required to be performed on-site . Work is performed on employer premises or designated assignment location. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: For Veterinary Nurse I: Completion of a two-year college program in veterinary and animal technology accredited by the American Veterinary Medical Association. For Veterinary Nurse II: Completion of a two-year college program in veterinary and animal technology accredited by the American Veterinary Medical Association and two years of relevant experience. For Veterinary Nurse III: Completion of a two-year college program in veterinary or animal technology accredited by the American Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA) and five years of relevant experience as a veterinary technician (RVT, LVT, CVT) after passing the Veterinary Technician National Exam. Preferred Qualifications: For All Veterinary Nurses: Knowledge of basic veterinary medical concepts, animal behavior and animal husbandry. Skilled in interpersonal and written communication. Skilled in basic computer skills. Be willing to master new techniques. Ability to handle, restrain, and provide medical treatments to domestic animals. Ability to adhere to appropriate safety procedures. Ability to multi-task and work in high intensity environment. Ability to perform general diagnostic procedures Skilled in time management and prioritizing daily responsibilities. Ability to work with and provide preventative maintenance for ordinary veterinary medical hospital equipment. For Veterinary Nurse II: Advanced knowledge of nursing care and assigned service requirements and policies. For Veterinary Nurse III: Ability to be a self-starter and be proactive in assisting others. Advanced knowledge of nursing care and assigned service requirements and policies. Other Requirements: Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Contact information for three professional references Application Window Closes on November 10, 2026. Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $18.04-34.69 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) e89291cd Last Name (required) 6f7bf733 Email (required) 8439ec61 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 39d505ae Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 859c15fe Last Name (required) 501d8c54 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 1f455c01 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 28cc915e Last Name (required) d3daffb8 Email (required) e3f3fffd Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job b74f3b9d Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for