    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/hr-representative-manhattan-kansas-united-states-3d7ee139-2db8-4399-b5c0-a0863a5d7490": {
      "title": "HR Representative",
      "description": "HR Representative - Manhattan, Kansas, United States HR Representative - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode HR Representative Apply Now HR Representative The Provost Business Office is searching for an HR Representative to serve our units under the Provost. 522412 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Provost Office Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position provides human resource activities for assigned reporting units served by the Provost Business Office team. Administrative services include compliance with university, State of Kansas and Federal policies, execution of the employee recruitment process, management of human resource payroll functions, time and leave, oversight of the performance management process, maintenance of employee records and providing benefits information all with a high level of excellent customer service. About Us The Office of the Provost provides administrative leadership for the university's academic enterprise, driving a culture of academic innovation and excellence in support of our Next-Gen K-State vision and goals. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and three years of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Associate degree or bachelor's degree in human resources. Two or more years of relevant experience in human resources and/or payroll. Experience in data entry, payroll, recruitment, human resources, and customer service. Excellent oral and written communication skills Excellent organizational skills Ability to determine priorities, exercise sound judgment and work independently Willingness to learn new software, to develop additional skills, and to engage in professional development Ability to exercise discretion and uphold confidentiality Demonstrated background or knowledge of human resource processes and policies Additional Role Information: Eligible to become a Notary Public upon employment Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter 3 Professional References Application Window Applications close on:November 6, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $18.04-23.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) f769f9f7 Last Name (required) 39f24d9b Email (required) 96b58323 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 8c673f7e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Human Resources Human Resources Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 9d57fba5 Last Name (required) 90a16445 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 0e94ac63 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) d6d90827 Last Name (required) a0cfb0ed Email (required) 75896e6a Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 9bef8477 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Extension Ag Econo