    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/faculty-position-in-industrial-design-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Industrial Design",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Industrial Design - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Faculty Position in Industrial Design - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Faculty Position in Industrial Design Apply Now Faculty Position in Industrial Design Join K-State’s Industrial Design program as a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor or Professor of Practice. Teach studios and courses in foundational design, furniture design, or visual communication. Starts Aug 2027. 522403 Manhattan 3670015040 Department of Design Academic / Faculty - 9 month Closing at: Jan 15 2027 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Industrial Design program at Kansas State University invites applications for a full-time, 9-month faculty position beginning August 2027. The successful candidate may be appointed as a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor or Professor of Practice, depending on qualifications, academic preparation, and professional experience. We seek a collaborative and forward-looking designer and educator who will contribute to the continued growth of our Industrial Design program. The successful candidate will bring expertise in contemporary design practice, a commitment to student learning, and new perspectives that help prepare the next generation of industrial designers. The program seeks candidates with demonstrated expertise in foundational design, furniture design, and/or visual communication. Candidates should be able to connect design education with evolving professional practice. TEACHING RESPONSIBILITIES The successful candidate will teach design studios and other courses across the Industrial Design curriculum, with assignments based on program needs and the candidate’s expertise. Candidates should be prepared to: Teach undergraduate studios and courses primarily and, as appropriate to the appointment, graduate design courses. Develop and teach lectures, seminars, and other courses in two of the following areas: foundational design, furniture design, or visual communication. Integrate contemporary design methods, tools, technologies, and industry practices into teaching. Maintain current course content and contribute to curriculum development and continuous program improvement. Collaborate with faculty, students, alumni, industry partners, and the broader design community. Support industry and community collaborations, internships, and career development opportunities that connect students with professional practice. APPOINTMENT PATHWAYS Tenure Track Assistant Professor The tenure-track appointment supports an integrated commitment to teaching, research and/or creative scholarship, and service. Teaching — 65–70% Teach undergraduate and graduate design studios and other courses aligned with the candidate’s expertise and program needs. Contribute to curriculum development, collaborative teaching, and the advancement of Industrial Design education. The teaching load is 14–16 credit hours per academic year, including 5-credit-hour studios and 2–3-credit-hour lectures or seminars. Research and Creative Scholarship — 25–30% Develop and sustain a focused program of research and/or creative scholarship informed by the candidate’s academic preparation, professional experience, teaching interests, or areas of design inquiry. Scholarly and creative work should advance Industrial Design and will form an important basis for promotion and tenure. Service — 5–10% Contribute to the program, department, college, university, profession, and broader community through committee participation, curriculum initiatives, professional engagement, outreach, and related activities. Professor of Practice The Professor of Practice appointment emphasizes teaching excellence, professional expertise, and engagement with the Industrial Design profession. Teaching — 80–90% Teach undergraduate Industrial Design studios and other courses aligned with the candidate’s professional expertise and program needs, including courses related to professional practice. Bring substantial practice experience into the classroom and connect student learning with current industry methods, expectations, and opportunities. The typical teaching load is 14–18 credit hours per academic year, including 5-credit-hour studios and 2–4-credit-hour lectures or seminars. Service — 10–20% Contribute to program, department, college, university, and community initiatives; student engagement; curriculum development; and professional communities. Strengthen relationships with alumni, industry partners, and employers, and identify opportunities for collaboration, internships, and student career development. About Us About Our Industrial Design Program The Industrial Design program is part of the Department of Design within Kansas State University’s College of Architecture, Planning, and Design. The program offers multiple pathways to the Master of Industrial Design degree. Students entering from high school complete a five-year non-baccalaureate master’s program, beginning with a foundation year in environmental studies and followed by four years of Industrial Design coursework, including a summer semester. Students with a previous bachelor’s degree may complete an accelerated graduate pathway in two to three years. The curriculum combines design exploration, human-centered design, prototyping, visual communication, professional preparation, and an award-winning Furniture Design sequence. Internship and study-abroad embedded experiences expand students’ academic and professional experience. Our goal is to prepare designers to address changing social, cultural, technological, and professional challenges through meaningful products, services, experiences, and systems. Faculty and students work in a collaborative interdisciplinary environment alongside Interior Architecture, Interior Design, Architecture, Landscape Architecture, and Regional and Community Planning. The department is housed in Seaton and Regnier Hall, with access to approximately 20,000 square feet of fabrication and research facilities supporting prototyping, experimentation, and hands-on learning. Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: For Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Required Qualifications Master’s degree or higher in Industrial Design, or a related field. Ability to teach undergraduate and graduate design studios across the curriculum. Ability to develop and teach lectures, seminars, or other courses related to the candidate’s expertise and program needs. Demonstrated excellence in written and visual communication appropriate to the design disciplines. Demonstrated potential to develop and sustain research and/or creative scholarship related to the candidate’s academic preparation, professional expertise, or areas of design inquiry. For Professor of Practice Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or higher in Industrial Design, Product Design, or related field. Six or more years of creative and/or professional practice experience in Industrial Design, Product Design, or a related field. Ability to teach undergraduate design studios across the curriculum. Ability to develop and teach courses related to professional practice in Industrial Design. Demonstrated excellence in written and visual communication appropriate to the design disciplines. The degree requirement is necessary for accreditation purposes and to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills, and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Preferred Qualifications: For Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Preferred Qualifications Six or more years of creative and/or professional practice experience in Industrial Design, Product Design, or a related field. Previous experience teaching at the university level. Evidence of an emerging or established research and/or creative scholarship agenda. Experience contributing to curriculum development. Record of service or engagement within academic, professional, or design communities. Experience collaborating with industry, community partners, or interdisciplinary teams. For Professor of Practice Preferred Qualifications Ten or more years of professional practice in Industrial Design, Product Design, or related field. Previous teaching experience in higher education. A diverse professional design background spanning multiple industries or product categories. Experience leading or collaborating with interdisciplinary design and development teams. Evidence of professional leadership, mentorship, or significant contribution to the Industrial Design profession. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents in one PDF: Letter of interest addressing your qualifications and interest in the position. Resume or curriculum vitae. Portfolio of professional and/or creative work. Teaching portfolio, if applicable. Application Window Applications close on: January 15, 2027 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $70,000-$78,000 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 5665fce8 Last Name (required) cd06c361 Email (required) 36b7ff86 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: d77b52e2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Education / Instructional Education / Instructional Employment Type Academic / Faculty - 9 month Academic / Faculty - 9 month Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 0ed8711c Last Name (required) 8c19e237 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later dd4ea362 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 365d994d Last Name (required) 05ffc7f8 Email (required) cda757ab Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 4c9410ba Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Graphic Designer Manhattan 3670006010 Div Comm and Mrktg Marketing & Member Strategist Other AQ Miller Schl of Media & Comm Landscape Technician II Manhattan Department of Housing & Dining Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusive community, dedicated to your professional growth. While specific benefits may vary by position, many roles come with comprehensive packages that support your well-being and work-life balance, including health and life insurance, retirement plans, and generous paid time off. To learn more about benefits that are available for various positions, visit our benefits overview page . Work Authorization and Sponsorship: Employees must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. International candidates who require employer-sponsored work authorization are welcome to apply. Eligibility for visa sponsorship depends on several factors, including but not limited to, the job’s occupational requirements, specific duties, wage level, the candidate’s qualifications (such as degree field) and available departmental resources. As a result, not all positions or applicants will be eligible for sponsorship. Equal Employment Opportunity: Kansas State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender identity, age, national origin, disability or status as a protected veteran. Remote and Hybrid work options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order to comply with all federal and state laws, filings, or tax requirements. Remote and hybrid work arrangements are not available for anyone who resides in the state of Idaho. Relocation to Kansas: Kansas participates in the MakeMyMove program, which connects eligible newcomers with participating communities offering financial incentives, housing support, and local perks to help make your move easier and more rewarding. If relocating from outside of Kansas you can visit the site to apply online for the program incentives. Background Screening Statement: Upon acceptance of a contingent offer of employment, a candidate may be subject to a background check per K-State’s background check policy . Interview Preferences: Kansas State University honors interview preferences for qualified applicants who are veterans or individuals with disabilities. Eligible applicants who meet the minimum qualifications, submit all required application materials, and submit required preference documentation by the closing date on the job advertisement will be granted a first-level interview. The disability and veteran interview preferences do not apply to student employment positions, temporary positions, athletics positions, academic and administrative department heads*, positions that require licensure as a physician, and positions that require that the employee be admitted to practice law in Kansas. *Heads of Departments refers to any individual holding a primary leadership role responsible for the overall strategic direction, management and operational oversight of a recognized academic or administrative unit within the university. To learn more about interview preferences at K-State, please visit our interview preferences page . Apply Now Already applied? Check the status of your application in your applicant portal . First Name (required) 43a097da Last Name (required) 0d1fce76 Email (required) 044fb1e8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Didn't find what you're looking for? Sign up to receive additional information about careers at K-State and a list of our recently posted jobs. First Name (required) 739cd876 Last Name (required) 0a2f7861 Email (required) 4d4e4a6b Sign up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose a worksite"
