    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/director-ii-enterprise-cloud-applications-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications",
      "description": "Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Apply Now Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications The Director of Enterprise Cloud Applications provides strategic leadership, technical guidance, and supervision for the Business Systems team. This team supports the university’s growing portfolio of SaaS and cloud-based business applications, including CRM, facilities, parking, and other administrative systems. This position serves as a hands-on technical leader, establishing development and support standards, defining best practices, and providing technical direction for Business Systems staff. Working in a highly collaborative environment, this position provides leadership to ensure system stability, service excellence, effective application lifecycle management, and alignment of the cloud application portfolio with institutional priorities and objectives. 522371 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Division of Info Tech Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Director of Enterprise Cloud Applications provides strategic leadership, technical guidance, and supervision for the Business Systems team. This team supports the university’s growing portfolio of SaaS and cloud-based business applications, including CRM, facilities, parking, and other administrative systems. This position serves as a hands-on technical leader, establishing development and support standards, defining best practices, and providing technical direction for Business Systems staff. Working in a highly collaborative environment, this position provides leadership to ensure system stability, service excellence, effective application lifecycle management, and alignment of the cloud application portfolio with institutional priorities and objectives. About Us Kansas State University's Division of Information Technology is committed to providing excellent IT services to the K-State community in support of the teaching, learning, research, and service missions. We offer a wide range of information, technology, and communications services. Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and ten years of relevant experience working with relational databases and SQL, and supporting system integrations, data extracts, or reporting solution. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in computer science or related field degree desired Knowledge of development, administration, and evaluations for cloud-based (SaaS) application systems Experience developing API’s in cloud application environments Excellent logical, analytical, and problem-solving skills Excellent oral and written communication skills Critical thinking ability Strong problem-solving capacity Attention to detail and results oriented Able to find root causes of problems and quickly determines efficient solutions Can anticipate risks and mitigate in the moment Comfortable under high-stress and exhibits poise and focus Ability to relate to diverse community of students, staff, and faculty High level of energy, enthusiasm, and ability to be innovative and creative Strong interpersonal skills Ability to read data models and flow diagrams. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Three Professional References Application Window Applications close on: November 6, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $79,926 - $105,894 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) ce88dd3e Last Name (required) f18276d4 Email (required) 9b1c736a Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 64cfa115 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Computer Science / Information Technology Computer Science / Information Technology Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 53e7fd20 Last Name (required) 32685ee3 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 1d726aba Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) c8d1f094 Last Name (required) 5bd20bf6 Email (required) 90f6f145 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job bbeef20c Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office IT Support Specialist II Manhattan Division of Info Tech Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. T