    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/associate-director-ii-zone-maintenance-manhattan-kansas-united-states-39e4f00b-5f12-4430-aa86-d38602cb46b6": {
      "title": "Associate Director II, Zone Maintenance",
      "description": "Associate Director II, Zone Maintenance - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Associate Director II, Zone Maintenance - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Associate Director II, Zone Maintenance Apply Now Associate Director II, Zone Maintenance This role will work to improve the overall day to day efficiency of the department through effectively using root cause analysis to provide strong tactical leadership to support facility maintenance across campus. Duties will require field assessment, monitoring and prioritizing work, planning/balancing preventative and reactive maintenance, scheduling and directing internal/external resources. Finally, the person in this role will be critical to providing Sr. Leadership and the campus community with data driven inputs to drive longer term facility planning. 522363 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fac Building Maintenance Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Nov 12 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Associate Director II, Zone Maintenance will assist the Director, Facilities Maintenance, and lead department supervision in the day-to-day management/leadership of the maintenance and renewal activities at Kansas State University. The person will provide overall leadership to a team of 50 departmental staff and direct supervision over five supervisors to ensure that the team is successful in safely completing work requests in a timely fashion with a keen focus on gold-standard customer service. This position requires a high level of dedication and campus on-site presence to include nights/weekends as needed. This role will work to improve the overall day to day efficiency of the department through effectively using root cause analysis to provide strong tactical leadership to support facility maintenance across campus. Duties will require field assessment, monitoring and prioritizing work, planning/balancing preventative and reactive maintenance, scheduling and directing internal/external resources. Finally, the person in this role will be critical to providing Sr. Leadership and the campus community with data driven inputs to drive longer term facility planning. About Us The Division of Facilities is an action-oriented service organization within the K-State family. We plan, budget, build, operate, maintain, clean, supply and transport. We are custodians, landscapers, carpenters, plumbers, electricians, mechanics, project managers, engineers, architects, accountants, and administrative professionals — all stewards and leaders of an inspiring campus shared by many. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and nine years of relevant experience in progressive supervision and leadership managing large complex operations such as physical plant, operations and/or skilled trades including responsibility for budget and financial management and performance management and analysis. Requirements may be met through a combination of work experience and education. Requires a valid driver’s license. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor Degree in Engineering, Architecture, Construction Management or related field. Professional Engineering License (PE) or master’s degree in architecture and/or Engineering District energy system (steam, chilled water) experience Clear examples of previous experience with the below: Provide vision and leadership in the management and direction of the organization. Examples of having a customer service mindset, style, and reputation, with the ability to influence others to adopt the same. Financial acumen to develop, review, and manage the department’s annual budget, performing cost and productivity analyses. Examples of benchmarking and measuring performance metrics internally and against similar organizations. Provide cost-effective maintenance and repair and renewal services, ensuring a safe, pleasant, and appropriate environment for all employees, students, and guests of the University with a strong emphasis on customer-oriented service. Recommending the implementation of new and revised operations and maintenance procedures or modifies the programs to maximize the efficient utilization of time, equipment, and manpower in the upkeep of physical campus infrastructure. Demonstrated experience of building and leading a diverse team towards a unified and well-articulated mission. Excellent communicator, both written and verbally, who can relate to a diverse population and establish a rapport based on trust. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Application Cover Letter Resume Application Window Applications close on: November 12, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $70,835 -$113,332 annually Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) f80f2b3d Last Name (required) e8115d85 Email (required) b96eb5dd Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: cc5d1fde Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative / Professional Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Administrative / Professional Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 457b49e8 Last Name (required) 9c4af05c Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 373c72e0 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) a0b70ed9 Last Name (required) 00203cb9 Email (required) f668b5cb Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 9ef51efd Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Why Join Us: Kansas State University offers a supportive and inclusi