    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/fire-inspector-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Fire Inspector",
      "description": "Fire Inspector - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fire Inspector - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Fire Inspector Apply Now Fire Inspector The position performs required inspections and testing of fire emergency equipment in compliance with state adopted fire codes. The position assists with assurance measures for other applicable State and Federal regulations and titles affecting higher education institutions. Position provides assistance with cursory inspection of key areas in compliance with regulations for life safety, occupational safety and health, and environmental protection, but the position's primary role is required in response to stipulations of the international fire code and additional fire safety requirements mandated by the State of Kansas. This position will assist senior personnel with ensuring environmental and industrial safety compliance assurance and laboratory safety by providing information during fire equipment inspections of key areas of concern and/or non-compliance to safety protocol to ensure that K-State is meeting Federal, State, local codes and regulations, and the expectations of accrediting bodies and funding entities as they pertain to environmental and safety matters 522338 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Environmental Health & Safety Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The position performs required inspections and testing of fire emergency equipment in compliance with state adopted fire codes. The position assists with assurance measures for other applicable State and Federal regulations and titles affecting higher education institutions. Position provides assistance with cursory inspection of key areas in compliance with regulations for life safety, occupational safety and health, and environmental protection, but the position's primarily role is required in response stipulations of the international fire code and additional fire safety requirements mandated by the State of Kansas. This position will assist senior personnel with ensuring environmental and industrial safety compliance assurance and laboratory safety by providing information during fire equipment inspections of key areas of concern and/or non-compliance to safety protocol to ensure that K-State is meeting Federal, State, local codes and regulations, and the expectations of accrediting bodies and funding entities as they pertain to environmental and safety matters. About Us The position performs required inspections and testing of fire emergency equipment in compliance with state adopted fire codes. The position assists with assurance measures for other applicable State and Federal regulations and titles affecting higher education institutions. Position provides assistance with cursory inspection of key areas in compliance with regulations for life safety, occupational safety and health, and environmental protection, but the position's primarily role is required in response stipulations of the international fire code and additional fire safety requirements mandated by the State of Kansas. This position will assist senior personnel with ensuring environmental and industrial safety compliance assurance and laboratory safety by providing information during fire equipment inspections of key areas of concern and/or non-compliance to safety protocol to ensure that K-State is meeting Federal, State, local codes and regulations, and the expectations of accrediting bodies and funding entities as they pertain to environmental and safety matters. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires two years of relevant experience and Fire Inspector I certification. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications: High School diploma or equivalent. Experience reading and interpreting fire code. Experience conducting building emergency system testing as described in the position duties. Familiarity with fire and life system systems. Basic experience with building electrical systems. Current 40 HazWoper certification. Experience in a higher education setting. Basic computer skills - (i.e., ability to use PC, laptops, tablets, and handheld barcode or other scanners. Able to download data from these systems. Able to use databases for entry and data look up. Able to communicate via email). Demonstrated verbal communication skills and excellent interpersonal skills. Self-motivated and able to work autonomously to complete required testing and inspection. Education or training in electrical/mechanical systems. Additional Role Information: Respond as needed for the Emergency Response Team. Post offer/pre-employment medical evaluation to assess and verify fitness for assigned duties (ability to climb and carry ladders and physical demands as described herein (i.e., physical demands section). Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover Letter Resume 3 References Application Window Applications close on: 11/06/2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $20.30 - $25.87/hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 29c74350 Last Name (required) 65449de8 Email (required) 9ddeac79 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 4dc90941 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Health & Safety H