      "title": "Instructor/Locum (Equine Surgery)",
      "description": "Instructor/Locum (Equine Surgery) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Instructor/Locum (Equine Surgery) - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Instructor/Locum (Equine Surgery) Apply Now Instructor/Locum (Equine Surgery) The Veterinary Health Center within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking applicants for a Locum Instructor in Equine Surgery. 522088 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Veterinary Health Center Temporary Part-time Closing at: Jun 15 2027 - 23:55 CDT On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Veterinary Health Center within the College of Veterinary Medicine is seeking applicants for a Locum Instructor in Equine Surgery. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: DVM The degree requirement is necessary for accreditation purposes and to ensure candidates possess the specialized knowledge, skills, and abilities that can only be attained through a formal educational program at this level. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Complete the application and submit a CV. Application Window Applications close on: 06/15/2027 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $1,200 daytime/nighttime or $1,800 daytime + emergency and travel expenses reimbursement Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) ec6a7a31 Last Name (required) c5e3f532 Email (required) 36dca76e Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 6a8e0b0e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of option