    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/assistant-director-of-athletics-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Athletics",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Athletics - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Assistant Director of Athletics - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Director of Athletics Apply Now Assistant Director of Athletics This position supports the financial and business operations of the athletics department and plays a key role in budgeting, financial reporting, business processes, and compliance. This position will contribute to sound fiscal management while supporting the mission and strategic goals of K-State Athletics. 521960 Manhattan, Kansas, United States K-State Athletics Inc (Agcy) Athletics On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role Kansas State Athletics invites applications for an Assistant/Associate Athletic Director of Business . This position supports the financial and business operations of a Power 4 intercollegiate athletics department and plays a key role in budgeting, financial reporting, business processes, and compliance. The successful candidate will contribute to sound fiscal management while supporting the mission and strategic goals of K-State Athletics. This position reports to the Senior Associate Athletic Director/Chief Financial Officer (or designee) and works collaboratively with athletics staff and campus partners. An example of job duties includes but are not limited to: Assist with the development, administration, and monitoring of the athletics department’s annual operating budget. Support daily business office operations, including purchasing, travel, contracts, payments, and internal controls. Support internal and external audits by preparing documentation and responding to audit requests Support financial processes related to evolving NCAA initiatives, including Name, Image, and Likeness (NIL), as applicable Supervise, train, and evaluate assigned business office staff and student employees. Assist with special projects, revenue initiatives, capital projects, and department modernization. • Perform other duties as assigned to support the goals and objectives of K-State Athletics. About Us K-State Athletics is a proud member of the Big 12 Conference. We are looking for someone who wants to become a member of our staff to help advance our program. Our mission is to foster a culture in which our student-athletes have every opportunity to reach their maximum potential academically, athletically, mentally and socially while operating an organization that is anchored by a genuine commitment to K-State, our supporters and each other. For more information on K-State Athletics, please visit http://www.kstatesports.com For more information on Manhattan, KS and the University, please visit http://www.k-state.edu/hcs/jobs/ Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in business administration, finance, accounting, sport management, or a related field. Minimum of five (5) years of progressively responsible experience in athletics business operations, higher education finance, or a related area. Demonstrated knowledge of NCAA and conference financial regulations. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in business administration, finance, sport management, or a related field. Experience working in a Power 4 (Power 5) intercollegiate athletics department. Supervisory or leadership experience. Experience using enterprise financial systems such as Workday, PeopleSoft, or similar platforms. Additional Role Information: Primarily an office-based position. Occasional evenings and weekends may be required based on athletics events and operational needs. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply To be considered for the position, please complete the online application and submit/upload the following documents: Cover letter indicating your qualifications for the position Resume with three professional references that includes contact information (name, title, phone number and email address) Application Window Screening of applications begins immediately and continues until the position is filled. Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $80,000 - $85,000 Benefits Excellent medical, dental and vision health plans Retirement plan (No Vesting Period!!) Generous earned leave plan – vacation and sick Parental leave plan Term life insurance Accidental death and dismemberment insurance Long term disability insurance Paid KSU designated holidays K-State Athletics Local Agency Employee Benefits Information: https://www.kstatesports.com/sports/2020/3/6/athletics-human-resources.aspx?path=resources Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 669c902d Last Name (required) a78bf02e Email (required) ec7e73f9 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 973a21c3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Athletics Business / Accounting / Finance Athletics Business / Accounting / Finance Employment Type Athletics Athletics Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 962fc5cd Last Name (required) 58a90885 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later a22e100b Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) ae01322b Last Name (required) d960fa30 Email (required) eb11dad5 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job f3ceea6c Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist (Accounts Receivable & Cashiering) Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Director II, Enterprise Cloud Applications Manhattan Division of Info Tech HR Manager Manhattan Provost Office Why Join Us: Discover a benefits package that truly prioritizes your well-being! Enjoy excellent medical, dental, and vision health plans, alongside a highly competitive retirement plan to secure your future. You’ll also benefit from earned vacation and sick leave, a generous parental leave plan, and robust insurance options, including term life, accidental death and dismemberment, and long-term disability coverage. Plus, take advantage of paid holidays designated by KSU, ensuring you have time to recharge and enjoy life to the fullest! K-State Athletics Local Agency Employee Benefits Information Work Authorization and Sponsorship: Employees must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of employment. International candidates who require employer-sponsored work authorization are welcome to apply. Eligibility for visa sponsorship depends on several factors, including but not limited to, the job’s occupational requirements, specific duties, wage level, the candidate’s qualifications (such as degree field) and available departmental resources. As a result, not all positions or applicants will be eligible for sponsorship. Remote and Hybrid work options: Some positions are eligible for remote or hybrid working arrangements. An employee who is working in a remote or hybrid capacity for K-State must reside within the United States in order