    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/landscape-technician-ii-manhattan-kansas-united-states-4527caec-5115-44bc-a601-66bac7abe805": {
      "title": "Landscape Technician II",
      "description": "Landscape Technician II - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Landscape Technician II - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Landscape Technician II Apply Now Landscape Technician II The role of the Grounds Maintenance and Landscape Department is to provide a safe, functional and aesthetically-pleasing exterior environment for the students, faculty and staff of Kansas State University. 521987 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fac Grounds Maintenance Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Dec 18 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position provides horticulture knowledge for completion of Grounds tasks and assistance in general Grounds maintenance. About Us The role of the Grounds Maintenance and Landscape Department is to provide a safe, functional and aesthetically-pleasing exterior environment for the students, faculty and staff of Kansas State University. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires six months of relevant experience. Education may be substituted for experience as determined relevant by a hiring manager. Valid driver's license Preferred Qualifications: Ability to write concise, meaningful reports. Perform mathematical computations necessary to make accurate estimates for supplies such as fertilizer, grass seed, flowers and chemicals, Knowledge and ability to use soil testing equipment. Ability to read and make recommendations from soil test results. Thorough knowledge of plant materials and accepted horticulture practices. Knowledge of methods, practices, techniques, and tools used in the planting and care of trees, shrubs, grasses, and plants. Knowledge of the hazards, proper use and effects insecticides and herbicides. Six months experience in equipment operation. High school graduate or equivalent. Training at post-secondary institution in nursery management, landscape horticulture, agronomy, horticulture, forestry, or plant pathology. Knowledge of all phases of horticultural practices preferred. Arborist training and experience in utilizing landscape plans and blueprint reading would be beneficial. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Application Application Window Applications close on: December 18, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range Hourly $15.00 - 16.52 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 6afc4594 Last Name (required) 2bf6e746 Email (required) 90adf0b1 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 06750fdc Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 02d6b30c Last Name (required) f63ce82d Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later e9203c35 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) a1dc101d Last Name (required) 88af5c3d Email (required) 804b7db1 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 8fcfa4d4 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks 