      "title": "Irrigation Technician I",
      "description": "Irrigation Technician I - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Irrigation Technician I - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Irrigation Technician I Apply Now Irrigation Technician I This position exists to provide grounds maintenance support for the campus. Performs basic repairs, installations, and maintenance for all irrigation systems. 521756 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fac Grounds Maintenance Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Dec 18 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Irrigation Technician I performs basic repairs, installations, and maintenance for all irrigation systems. Performs preventative and routine maintenance on irrigation systems and assists in irrigation repairs and troubleshooting. About Us The role of the Landscape Services is to provide a safe, functional and aesthetically pleasing exterior environment for the students, faculty and staff of K-State. The department is responsible for the maintenance and installation of over 250 acres of turf grass, shrubs, trees and annual flower beds on campus. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma and one year of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Valid driver's license Preferred Qualifications: Skill in use and operations of tools, machines and equipment commonly used in plumbing and electrical work at the skilled craft level. 1-3 years of experience in irrigation system installation and maintenance Institution grounds experience Additional Role Information: Back flow Certification must be completed within first year of employment. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Application Application Window Applications close on: December 18, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range Hourly $15.00 - $18.17 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 0d51ae8d Last Name (required) 227fd805 Email (required) 02603946 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 4efde28b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) a554accc Last Name (required) 7b7ab81d Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 8ff2e80f Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 537b94ba Last Name (required) 518be3b4 Email (required) 3d299dd9 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job f953f0e2 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist Manhattan Vet Med Support Services IT Support Specialist I Manhattan Arts & Sciences Dean Office Custodial Specialist Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playbac