      "title": "IT Support Specialist I",
      "description": "IT Support Specialist I - Manhattan, Kansas, United States IT Support Specialist I - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode IT Support Specialist I Apply Now IT Support Specialist I The College of Arts and Sciences is seeking qualified applicants for an IT Support Specialist I position. This role will provide IT services and technical support to departments across the College. 522465 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Arts & Sciences Dean Office Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Nov 15 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The IT Support Specialist I will provide IT services within the College of Arts & Sciences. This position is responsible for ensuring printing technology is operational for all users, assisting with technology development and documentation, maintaining records, and supporting the development of workstation imaging and computer setup processes. About Us The College of Arts & Sciences is home to 20 departments that span the arts and humanities, social and behavioral sciences, and natural and quantitative sciences. An arts and sciences education prepare students for a lifetime of career success, professional responsibility, and personal fulfillment while enriching society. The college teaches critical thinking, promotes understanding of how the world works, and provides opportunities to imagine a better future. Learn more at https://artsci.k-state.edu/ Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: • Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent) and one year of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science and/or 