    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/registered-nurse-manhattan-kansas-united-states-3a94fd84-dfa9-4b88-9f0b-3c829f18e5d8": {
      "title": "Registered Nurse",
      "description": "Registered Nurse - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Registered Nurse - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Registered Nurse Apply Now Registered Nurse Lafene Health Center is looking for a highly dedicated and enthusiastic Allergy & Immunization Registered Nurse. 522268 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Lafene Student Health Center Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Nov 17 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role Individual in this position provides nursing care to patients who present for care daily in the Allergy & Immunization department. Duties include but are not limited to: Assessing patient needs through interviewing, recognizing and interpreting symptoms and conditions in order to determine individual response to treatment program and current medication. This is done in order to prepare, record, and relay accurate reports on the status of the patient's progress to the treating physician and staff members directly involved in total care of the patient. Administration of medications and treatments as prescribed. Instructing patient regarding self-care techniques and preventive strategies. This is done by evaluating level of understanding of disease process and /or potential health status, providing information needed and determining the patient's intent for compliance with the treatment routine. Written and verbal instructions maybe given. This is done in order to promote the highest level of physical, mental well-being possible. Formulating nursing diagnoses in order to outline a nursing care plan specific to the patient's needs. This is to insure continuity of medical, physical, and emotional care during the treatment process. Two positions are available a 9-month position and a 12-month position. About Us Lafene Health Center provides students with accessible, high-quality, and affordable outpatient healthcare, focusing on keeping students healthy and promoting a healthy campus community. Care is provided by board-certified physicians, nurse practitioners, and nursing professionals, ensuring students receive the same high-quality care they would expect from their healthcare providers at home. Students have access to coordinated and comprehensive services designed to build and maintain their overall well-being. We believe that good health is essential for academic success. The mission of Lafene Health Center at Kansas State University is to offer accessible, high-quality, affordable outpatient healthcare services on the Manhattan campus while also providing exceptional health and well-being education to the student body and the larger Kansas State University community. This mission is guided by the Health Center's core values of compassion, mutual respect, adherence to evidence-based healthcare and university standards, appreciation for timeliness, and collaboration, which ensures students receive respectful, efficient, and comprehensive care while fostering the best possible healthcare experience. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Must be licensed to practice as a registered nurse (RN) in the state of Kansas. Preferred Qualifications: Graduate of an approved school of professional nursing. 2-3 years experience in performing health assessments, allergy injections and immunizations. 2-3 years experience in executing organizational policy, goals or objectives. At the time of appointment the selected employee must possess a Kansas licensure/temporary permit, or be given authority to practice as a Registered Nurse (RN) by the Kansas State Board of Nursing. Must comply with Kansas Board of Nursing requirements for licensing renewal, i.e., provide proof of participation in at least 30 hours of continuing education every two (2) years, complete application and submit fee. Possess current CPR certification upon employment and update every two years. Mandatory participation in continuing education courses and in-service sessions in order to continually update nursing knowledge, skills, and abilities. Mobility to move about the general clinic rapidly, standing for several hours performing nursing functions in confined spaces. Manual dexterity to give injections and other duties requiring fine motor skills. Assist clients who are fainting by giving physical support to prevent injury and/or to assist in lifting or moving a client. Physical ability to perform CPR as necessary until relieved by other staff or paramedics. AED unit, ambu bag, audiometer, biology, blood pressure cuff, cast cutter, cyro-surgical equipment, ear irrigator, gomco suction, gurney, halogen light, opthalmascope/otoscope, oxygen tank & gauge, personal computer, pulse oximeter, scales, spirometer, stethoscope, surgical instruments, syringe, telephone, thermometer, titmus vision tester, wheelchair. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Three Professional References Application Window Applications close on: November 17, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $28.00 - $33.00 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 43035b71 Last Name (required) af9cf965 Email (required) 4bacbfb0 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: a4a5571c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Health Profession Health Profession Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) fa02d774 Last Name (required) 8d8bc3cf Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later fbe98cfa Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 267a1c6a Last Name (required) 6d69a072 Email (required) 350e54ab Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job f84cbf0b Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist Manhattan Vet Med Support Services IT Support Specialist I Manhattan Arts & Sciences Dean Office Custodial Specialist Manhattan Vet Med Support Services Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:46 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:46 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Captions captions settings , opens captions settings dialog captions off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Why Join Us: Kansas Stat