    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/recruitment-program-specialist-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Recruitment Program Specialist",
      "description": "Recruitment Program Specialist - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Recruitment Program Specialist - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Recruitment Program Specialist Apply Now Recruitment Program Specialist This position supports the Office of Recruitment and Admissions by coordinating recruitment travel and off-site activities, managing travel expenses and reimbursements, and providing administrative and program support. 522463 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Recruitment and Admissions Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Nov 20 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role The Office of Recruitment and Admissions at Kansas State University is seeking an organized, detail-oriented, and collaborative individual to provide administrative and program coordination support for undergraduate recruitment activities. This position plays an important role in supporting the university's recruitment and enrollment goals by working closely with recruitment staff to plan, coordinate, and execute off-campus recruitment activities, including high school visits, college fairs, and other outreach initiatives. Responsibilities include coordinating recruitment travel logistics, assisting with travel planning and arrangements, managing travel-related expenses and reimbursements, and ensuring appropriate documentation and compliance with university policies and procedures. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with recruitment staff and campus partners to support efficient operations, facilitate the effective use of resources, and help ensure recruitment activities are well-organized and successfully executed. The position requires strong organizational skills, attention to detail, effective communication, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced, team-oriented environment. About Us Recruitment and Admissions promotes student success by engaging future, new and current students and families with the K-State community in a spirit of inclusivity, collaboration, and excellence. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires one year of relevant experience. Requirements may be met through a combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Experience developing travel procedures, reports, and program metrics. Experience preparing travel expense reports. Strong organizational, planning, and time management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Excellent written and verbal communication skills and the ability to work effectively with customers, government representatives, and cross-functional teams. Demonstrated ability to work independently while supporting a collaborative team environment. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Three Professional References Application Window Applications close on: November 20,2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $ 14.54 - $18.17 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 4a43365d Last Name (required) fcab69b7 Email (required) e3ad1dce Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 45771ab5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic Advising / Support Administrative / Professional Student Affairs / Services Academic Advising / Support Administrative / Professional Student Affairs / Services Employmen