    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/director-of-pre-college-and-enrollment-partnerships-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Director of Pre-College and Enrollment Partnerships",
      "description": "Director of Pre-College and Enrollment Partnerships - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Director of Pre-College and Enrollment Partnerships - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Director of Pre-College and Enrollment Partnerships Apply Now Director of Pre-College and Enrollment Partnerships This position provides strategic leadership for the development, implementation, and expansion of pre-college programs and enrollment partnerships that advance Kansas State University’s enrollment goals and create accessible pathways to higher education. The position oversees concurrent enrollment, dual-credit, dual-admission, and other innovative educational pathways designed to strengthen student recruitment, college readiness, and transitions to degree-seeking programs. Working collaboratively with university offices, including Undergraduate Admissions, the Division of Academic Success and Student Affairs, Office of the Registrar, Office of Student Financial Assistance, Graduate School, and academic colleges, this position supports coordinated recruitment, enrollment, and student success strategies 522461 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Vice Provost Enrollment Mgmt Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Closing at: Nov 25 2026 - 23:55 CST Hybrid eligible Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position provides strategic leadership for the development, implementation, and expansion of pre-college programs and enrollment partnerships that advance Kansas State University’s enrollment goals and create accessible pathways to higher education. The position oversees concurrent enrollment, dual-credit, dual-admission, and other innovative educational pathways designed to strengthen student recruitment, college readiness, and transitions to degree-seeking programs. Working collaboratively with university offices, including Undergraduate Admissions, the Division of Academic Success and Student Affairs, Office of the Registrar, Office of Student Financial Assistance, Graduate School, and academic colleges, this position supports coordinated recruitment, enrollment, and student success strategies. The position builds and sustains strategic partnerships with K-12 school districts, community colleges, industry leaders, and community organizations to expand educational opportunities, strengthen enrollment pipelines, and align academic pathways with student interests and workforce needs at the regional and national levels. Worksite Description This position is Hybrid eligible . 3 days a week in office in Manhattan, KS. All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a bachelor's degree and five years of relevant experience. Education beyond the minimum degree requirement may count toward required experience if deemed relevant by the hiring manager. The degree requirement ensures candidates possess the strategic, financial, leadership and operational skills essential for directing complex academic student services functions. These competencies are typically developed and validated only through the comprehensive curriculum and experiential learning inherent in a formal degree program. Preferred Qualifications: Master's Degree 5-7 years of secondary school experience highly preferred High school administration experience preferred Experience partnering with community colleges and technical schools Strong communication skills for effective internal and external relationship development Self-motivated and detail oriented, able to work independently Ability to work effectively with individuals from various backgrounds and educational levels Strong qualitative and quantitative analytic skills and experience using data to inform decisions Evidence of effective budgetary management Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Resume Cover Letter Three Professional References Application Window Applications close on: November 25, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $61,591 - $98,555 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 7a9e18e5 Last Name (required) bd06f43e Email (required) b47e3f41 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 00b59469 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic Advising / Support Executive / Director / Management Student Affairs / Services Academic Advising / Support Executive / Director / Management Student Affairs / Services Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Regular) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite Hybrid eligible Hybrid eligible Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) cc71bc07 Last Name (required) 7178d09b Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 92925518 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) c715e71f Last Name (required) a2c5e1f5 Email (required) 1d3dc166 Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 8c1fb341 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist Manhattan Vet Med Support Services IT Support Specialist I Manhattan Arts & Sciences Dean Office Custodial Specialist Manhattan Vet Med Support S