    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/maintenance-and-repair-tech-ii-manhattan-kansas-united-states-eae4cb30-a948-46f1-9ef0-0eb00ecb2b9f": {
      "title": "Maintenance and Repair Tech II",
      "description": "Maintenance and Repair Tech II - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Maintenance and Repair Tech II - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Maintenance and Repair Tech II Apply Now Maintenance and Repair Tech II This position performs preventative maintenance, repairs and service work on machinery, equipment, vehicles, tools, and buildings including but not limited to HVAC, plumbing and electrical support. 521900 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Fac Building Maintenance Staff Full Time (USS) Closing at: Dec 18 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role This position exists to perform skilled preventive maintenance to building equipment in a large university setting. Coordinates with other technicians and trades employees to diagnose problems and refers issues requiring specialized training. About Us The Division of Facilities' maintenance personnel conduct routine maintenance on building systems and equipment to ensure the operational reliability of our campus' building systems. This maintenance involves regular, scheduled service to maintain equipment functionality without the need for immediate repairs. Many of the older buildings have systems and equipment that have exceeded their expected lifespan, highlighting the value of a strong preventive maintenance program. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires one year of relevant experience. Various training and/or certification may be required. Education may be substituted for experience as determined relevant by a hiring manager. Valid driver's license Preferred Qualifications: Prefer ability to troubleshoot and possess the hands-on experience with industrial type exhaust fans, air handling units, heating/cooling ventilation, change and rewire ballasts, and utilize wiring diagrams to install according to manufacturers’ specifications. Prefer ability to read, understand, and work from wiring diagrams. High school graduate or equivalent is preferred. Four years of experience in the mechanical or building trades or crafts, including at least two years of experience in two separate mechanical or building trades. At least two years of experience in mechanical, heating/cooling ventilation (no certification), electrical, carpentry, and/or plumbing is preferred. Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship. How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Application Application Window Applications close on: December 18, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $17.00 hourly Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) cdacd08d Last Name (required) 88154e84 Email (required) 95d67faa Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 13e489d0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Custodial / Landscaping / Maintenance Employment Type Staff Full Time (USS) Staff Full Time (USS) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) f8b6cbfe Last Name (required) f5c8ca41 Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 55d3809c Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) f0c2