    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/research-assistant-manhattan-kansas-united-states-1bd33e0a-8c54-4184-a42a-86c267e4dc75": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Research Assistant - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Research Assistant - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Research Assistant Apply Now Research Assistant We are seeking a highly motivated and detail-oriented Research Assistant to support research activities in vaccine development and evaluation. This position works under the guidance and supervision of a senior research scientist and plays a critical role in experimental planning, execution, and laboratory operations. 521383 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Anatomy & Physiology Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Nov 15 2026 - 09:45 CST On-site Add to favorites View favorites About This Role We are seeking a highly motivated and detail-oriented Research Assistant to support research activities in vaccine development and evaluation. This position works under the guidance and supervision of a senior research scientist and plays a critical role in experimental planning, execution, and laboratory operations. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a bachelor's degree. (Education beyond the minimum degree requirement may count toward required experience if deemed relevant by the hiring manager.) The degree requirement ensures candidates possess the advanced theoretical knowledge, highly specialized methodologies, and critical problem-solving skills fundamental to this work. These competencies are typically developed and rigorously validated only through the comprehensive curriculum and intensive experiential experience inherent in a formal degree program. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in microbiology, immunology, virology, animal science, biology, or a related field Hands-on laboratory experience with cell culture and molecular techniques Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Please submit the following documents: 1. Cover letter 2. Resume 3. Contact information of three professional references Application Window Applications close on: November 15, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range Hourly $ 20.00 - 32.05 Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) cd22ad92 Last Name (required) 1cbae49c Email (required) 582643d9 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 3d42cea3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research / Scientific / Grants Veterinary Medicine Research / Scientific / Grants Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 6a143c72 Last Name (required) 6888535b Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later e8583ac7 Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 39b30d93 Last Name (required) c513ebe5 Email (required) 653cf19b Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job 39007ca3 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for sharing this job! You may also be interested in Accounting Specialist Manhattan Vet Med Support Services IT Support Specialist I Manhattan Arts & Sciences Dean Office