    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/research-associate-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Research Associate - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Research Associate - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Research Associate Apply Now Research Associate We are seeking a highly motivated and experienced Research Associate to contribute to multiple vaccine development and evaluation projects. Working with minimal supervision from the Principal Investigator, this position requires independent experimental design and execution, strong technical expertise, and the ability to coordinate team-based research activities. 521382 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Anatomy & Physiology Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Closing at: Nov 15 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site About This Role We are seeking a highly motivated and experienced Research Associate to contribute to multiple vaccine development and evaluation projects. Working with minimal supervision from the Principal Investigator, this position requires independent experimental design and execution, strong technical expertise, and the ability to coordinate team-based research activities. Worksite Description This position is On-site . All employees must reside in the United States when they begin working to comply with state law. K-State is unable to provide remote or hybrid work opportunities for residents of the state of Idaho. What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a master's degree and two years of relevant experience. (Education beyond the minimum degree requirement may count toward required experience if deemed relevant by the hiring manager.) The degree requirement ensures candidates possess advanced research skills, data analysis expertise and scientific writing ability in order to independently execute complex research tasks, interpret findings and contribute to scholarly publications. These competencies are typically developed and rigorously validated only through the comprehensive curriculum and intensive experiential learning inherent in a formal degree program. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree (or higher) in microbiology, immunology, virology, animal science, biology, or a related field Or BS degree with demonstrated hands-on experience in cell culture, molecular biology, and immunoassays Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: 1. Cover letter 2. Resume 3. Contact information of three professional references Application Window Applications close: November 15, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $50,000 - $70,000 annually Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 79405064 Last Name (required) 29571ce7 Email (required) c4e29c35 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 4add251f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research / Scientific / Grants Veterinary Medicine Research / Scientific / Grants Veterinary Medicine Employment Type Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Staff Full Time (Unclassified - Term) Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) 96b9965a Last Name (required) 295b059f Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later 07ef94bf Save Now! Please wait... Done Not You? We sent this job to you Share this job with a friend First Name (required) 07b619ca Last Name (required) a8b3542a Email (required) d00b153d Provide your friend's name and email and we'll send this job aa1ca1b0 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? Thanks for s