    "https://careers.k-state.edu/jobs/research-aide-manhattan-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Research Aide",
      "description": "Research Aide - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Research Aide - Manhattan, Kansas, United States Kiosk mode Research Aide Apply Now Research Aide The Division of Biology seeks Field Research Aides to collect data for research projects, with start dates of January 4, 2027, or February 22, 2027. 522466 Manhattan, Kansas, United States Biology Temporary Full-time Closing at: Nov 30 2026 - 23:55 CST On-site About This Role The Division of Biology is hiring Temporary Full-Time Research Aides for seasonal ecology research projects in Kansas. Research objectives will be focused on collecting data on avian survival, nest success, brood survival, habitat selection, and movements on landscapes among six separate study areas. Project-related field equipment/vehicles will be provided for project staff assigned to each study area team. Teams will consist of 2–3 technicians led by a project researcher. Field activities will be supervised by a lead technician and/or graduate student. About Us The Division of Biology at Kansas State University is composed of a dynamic group of tenure-track, research, and instructional faculty, as well as a large number of postdoctoral research associates, graduate students, and support staff. All of these individuals are essential to accomplish the Division of Biology's mission, to generate and disseminate high-quality biological scientific knowledge through teaching, research, service, and outreach. The research, teaching, and service interests of these individuals are varied, spanning all areas of biological research, teaching and training at the postdoctoral, graduate, and undergraduate levels, as well as service and outreach contributions to the broader scientific community and the public. Worksite Description This position is On-site . What You'll Need to Succeed Minimum Qualifications: Requires a high school diploma (or equivalent). Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications: Strong work ethic and willingness to learn Ability to follow established project protocols Ability to communicate effectively with project staff, collaborators, and diverse stakeholders Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Ability to carry trapping equipment over rough terrain in inclement weather Interest in applied wildlife conservation and growing as a wildlife professional Willingness to work early mornings (pre-dawn) and long hours in cold and hot weather Must possess a valid US driver’s license without restrictions Experience in wildlife capture and handling Some plant ID experience Experience driving 4WD vehicles, UTVs, and ATVs The completion or pursuit of a bachelor's degree in wildlife management, biology, or closely related discipline Experience and interest in plant and invertebrate identification Sponsorship eligibility: Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the U.S. on an ongoing basis without sponsorship How to Apply Please submit the following documents: Cover letter Resume Application Window Applications close on: November 30, 2026 Anticipated Hiring Pay Range $14.00- $16.00 per hour Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 9de16574 Last Name (required) 02fbdeb6 Email (required) a18a5b66 Select one or more from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs: 942c3f5e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research / Scientific / Grants Research / Scientific / Grants Employment Type Temporary Full-time Temporary Full-time Locations Manhattan, Kansas, United States Manhattan, Kansas, United States Worksite On-site On-site Sign Up! Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Save this job for later Add this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later Save this job to your favorites or send it to yourself to apply later (required) ffbc2